ca-06017-bos-matter-40966.title:
Health and Human Services Agency (HHSA) recommending the Board:
1) Make findings pursuant to Section 3.13.030 (G) of the El Dorado County Ordinance Chapter 3.13, Contracting Out, that the veterinary services provided by Animal Outreach of the Mother Lode involve urgent or emergency services;
2) Make findings in accordance with Procurement Policy C-17 Section 3.6.G(1) exempting the competitive bidding process with Purchasing Agent concurrence because, "There is only one provider capable of providing the product or service that satisfies the department's operational requirements, because of the technological, specialized, or unique character, or proprietary nature, and therefore it is not possible to obtain competitive bids";
3) Approve and authorize the Chair to sign Agreement for Services 10491 with Animal Outreach of the Mother Lode, with an amount not to exceed $250,000, and for the term of three years from January 1, 2027 through December 31, 2029;
4) Authorize the Purchasing Agent to execute amendments relating to Agreement 10491, contingent upon approval by County Counsel and Risk Management, which do not increase the maximum dollar amount or term of the Agreement; and
5) Authorize the HHSA Director, or the Chief Assistant Director, to execute programmatic, administrative, and fiscal documents relating to Agreement 10491.

FUNDING: 15% Fees for Services, 9% Licensing/Permit Fees, 7% Public Health Realignment, and 69% General Fund. In some cases, 100% Pet Aid Special Revenue Fund.

ca-06017-bos-matter-41049.title:
Procurement and Contracts, a division of the Chief Administrative Office, recommending the Board:
1) Make findings that it is appropriate to engage an independent contractor to provide as-needed confidential document and electronic waste destruction services, as Agreement 10418, requires specialty skills and qualifications not expressly identified in County classifications, in accordance with County ordinance code 3.13.030 (B); 
2) Award Request for Proposals 2025-0174 to CEAR, LLC doing business as California Electronic Asset Recovery;
3) Approve and authorize the Purchasing Agent to execute Agreement for Services 10418 with CEAR, LLC dba California Electronic Asset Recovery, for a total agreement  amount of $150,000, for a term to become effective upon execution by both parties and expiring three years thereafter, to provide as-needed confidential document and electronic waste destruction services; and
4) Authorize the Purchasing Agent to execute amendments relating to Agreement 10418, contingent upon approval by County Counsel and Risk Management, which do not increase the maximum dollar amount or term of the Agreement. 

FUNDING:  Various, as departments have included appropriations for document and electronic waste destruction services in their respective budgets.

